    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n26314" root="طبع" body-key="T">
    
      2 
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">طبّع</span></b> , inf. n. <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">تَطْبِيعٌ</span>, <i>He sealed well</i> [or <i>much,</i>
or <i>he sealed</i> a number of writings &amp;c.]. (KL: in
which only the inf. n. is mentioned.) ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b2-  And <i>He
loaded</i> [a beast <i>heavily,</i> or] <i>well.</i> (KL.) ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b3-  See
also 1, a little after the middle. ＝   
    <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer1"> </span>-A2-  <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">تَطْبِيعٌ</span> signifies
also The <i>rendering unclean, dirty, filthy,</i> or
<i>impure.</i> (O, K.) ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b2-  See 1, last sentence.

